=B. "civic life depends on people"#Correct. This directly supports the idea that participation matters to civic life. Notice how the answer uses the exact wording, evidence, or concept required by the standard.
~C. "silence with participation"#Incorrect. This names the contrast but not the full meaning. Recheck the passage, context, or task wording and choose the option that preserves meaning and matches the standard.
~D. "willing to speak and listen"#Incorrect. This is relevant, but it is less complete than the phrase about civic life depending on people.
}

